# 45 fashion brands: (slug, name, url, verified fact, observation 1, observation 2, slide notes [(text, fx, fy)])
# fx/fy = where the note's line points, as a fraction of the logo's visible bounds.
B=[
("gucci","Gucci","https://www.gucci.com/","Guccio Gucci founded the house in Florence in 1921, and the interlocking GG monogram was introduced in the 1960s.","Two mirrored G's lock together into a single round mark, built from the founder's initials.","A light, classic serif wordmark sits above the monogram, so the symbol does the heavy lifting.",[("Guccio Gucci initials",0.3,0.72),("classic serif",0.5,0.08),("mirrored G's",0.8,0.75)]),
("louis-vuitton","Louis Vuitton","https://www.louisvuitton.com/","Louis Vuitton opened his Paris trunk workshop in 1854, and his son Georges created the LV monogram canvas in 1896.","The serif L and V overlap so tightly that they read as one letterform.","The full name is set tiny underneath, because the monogram is recognized on its own.",[("interlocking L + V",0.35,0.35),("serif cuts",0.75,0.1),("tiny wordmark",0.5,0.97)]),
("chanel","Chanel","https://www.chanel.com/","Gabrielle \"Coco\" Chanel opened her first boutique in Paris in 1910, and the house still signs everything with this bold geometric wordmark.","Wide, geometric capitals give the name a modern, architectural feel that has barely changed in a century.","Generous letter spacing and pure black make it look confident without any symbol.",[("wide geometric caps",0.15,0.5),("pure black",0.6,0.15),("generous spacing",0.8,0.85)]),
("hermes","Hermès","https://www.hermes.com/","Thierry Hermès founded the company as a harness workshop in Paris in 1837, and the Duc carriage logo has been used since the 1950s.","The horse-drawn carriage tells the brand's origin story: it started by making harnesses and saddles.","Notably, the carriage has no driver, which is often read as the brand providing the craft and the customer taking the reins.",[("Duc carriage",0.5,0.12),("harness-maker roots",0.12,0.18),("slab serif",0.5,0.62)]),
("prada","Prada","https://www.prada.com/","Mario Prada and his brother opened their leather goods shop in Milan's Galleria Vittorio Emanuele II in 1913.","The flared serif capitals and the R with its curled leg make the wordmark instantly recognizable.","The wide, heavy letters feel like an engraved shop sign, a nod to the brand's 1913 Milan store.",[("curled R leg",0.5,0.92),("wide caps",0.12,0.3),("Milan since 1913",0.85,0.3)]),
("dior","Dior","https://www.dior.com/","Christian Dior founded his couture house in Paris in 1946 and launched the famous New Look the following year.","High-contrast Didone letters, with very thin and very thick strokes, signal couture and elegance.","Dropping \"Christian\" leaves four tall letters that work as a monogram and a wordmark at once.",[("high contrast",0.15,0.3),("Didone serif",0.5,0.08),("four letters",0.85,0.85)]),
("fendi","Fendi","https://www.fendi.com/","Adele and Edoardo Fendi founded the brand in Rome in 1925, and Karl Lagerfeld designed the FF \"Zucca\" monogram in 1965.","The double F mark, one letter flipped, creates a compact pattern that also works as a print.","A heavy, condensed sans serif wordmark makes Fendi feel more modern than most Italian houses.",[("FF by Lagerfeld",0.5,0.12),("condensed sans",0.18,0.8),("Roman house",0.85,0.8)]),
("versace","Versace","https://www.versace.com/","Gianni Versace founded the house in Milan in 1978 and chose the Medusa head from Greek mythology as its emblem.","Medusa represents fatal attraction: a mythological figure who made everyone who looked at her fall under her spell.","The widely spaced serif capitals keep the classical theme going below the emblem.",[("Medusa head",0.35,0.2),("Greek key border",0.75,0.3),("spaced serif",0.5,0.92)]),
("burberry","Burberry","https://www.burberry.com/","Thomas Burberry founded the company in 1856, and in 2023 the brand returned to a serif wordmark and its Equestrian Knight emblem.","The 2023 serif wordmark replaced the plain sans serif from 2018, bringing back a sense of British heritage.","Narrow, tall capitals give the name a classic, tailored feel, like the trench coat it is famous for.",[("2023 serif",0.3,0.15),("British heritage",0.75,0.15),("narrow caps",0.5,0.9)]),
("givenchy","Givenchy","https://www.givenchy.com/","Hubert de Givenchy founded his house in Paris in 1952, and the 4G monogram dates from the brand's early years.","Four square G's are arranged into a grid that reads like a modern, almost architectural emblem.","The spaced sans serif wordmark under the mark keeps the whole logo clean and graphic.",[("4G monogram",0.3,0.25),("square G's",0.85,0.4),("spaced caps",0.5,0.95)]),
("balenciaga","Balenciaga","https://www.balenciaga.com/","Cristóbal Balenciaga opened his first house in San Sebastián, Spain, in 1917 and moved to Paris in 1937.","The 2017 wordmark is a wide sans serif with stretched letters, similar to the style used on bus stops and signage.","Removing all decoration makes the logo feel provocative and almost anti-luxury, which suits the brand.",[("wide sans",0.18,0.5),("stretched letters",0.6,0.15),("anti-luxury",0.85,0.85)]),
("saint-laurent","Saint Laurent","https://www.ysl.com/","Yves Saint Laurent founded the house in Paris in 1961, and in 2012 creative director Hedi Slimane renamed the ready-to-wear line Saint Laurent.","The bold Helvetica-style wordmark replaced \"Yves Saint Laurent\" for the ready-to-wear line.","The famous YSL monogram by Cassandre still exists for bags and beauty, so the wordmark can stay plain.",[("\"Yves\" removed",0.18,0.25),("bold sans",0.6,0.15),("YSL still on bags",0.85,0.88)]),
("celine","Celine","https://www.celine.com/","Céline Vipiana founded the brand in Paris in 1945, and in 2018 Hedi Slimane removed the accent from the name.","Dropping the accent on the É made the name look cleaner and more international.","Wide, round letters with even spacing give the wordmark a calm, confident look.",[("accent removed",0.18,0.1),("wide letters",0.55,0.9),("Slimane, 2018",0.88,0.35)]),
("valentino","Valentino","https://www.valentino.com/","Valentino Garavani founded the house in Rome in 1960, and the V in an oval is the brand's signature emblem.","The serif V inside an oval works like a seal or a monogram on hardware and packaging.","The brand uses the founder's first name, set in classic Roman serif capitals.",[("V in an oval",0.5,0.15),("Roman serif",0.18,0.85),("first name only",0.82,0.92)]),
("giorgio-armani","Giorgio Armani","https://www.armani.com/","Giorgio Armani and Sergio Galeotti founded the company in Milan in 1975.","Very condensed, thin capitals make the full name fit in one elegant line.","The understated type matches Armani's reputation for soft tailoring and quiet colors.",[("condensed caps",0.18,0.4),("thin strokes",0.6,0.15),("understated",0.82,0.85)]),
("dolce-and-gabbana","Dolce & Gabbana","https://www.dolcegabbana.com/","Domenico Dolce and Stefano Gabbana founded the brand in Milan in 1985.","The two founders' surnames sit side by side, joined by a tiny ampersand.","A bold, geometric sans serif keeps the long name readable on labels and storefronts.",[("two founders",0.15,0.3),("tiny ampersand",0.47,0.75),("bold sans",0.85,0.8)]),
("bottega-veneta","Bottega Veneta","https://www.bottegaveneta.com/","Bottega Veneta was founded in Vicenza, Italy, in 1966, and is known for its woven intrecciato leather.","The spaced serif capitals are quiet, which suits a brand famous for having no visible logo on its bags.","Its old slogan, \"When your own initials are enough\", explains why the logo stays so modest.",[("spaced serif",0.18,0.3),("quiet luxury",0.6,0.15),("logo-free bags",0.82,0.88)]),
("loewe","Loewe","https://www.loewe.com/","Loewe was founded in Madrid in 1846, which makes it one of the oldest luxury houses in the world.","The 2014 wordmark, made under creative director Jonathan Anderson, uses a refined serif with flared strokes.","The round O stands out between straight letters, giving the short name its rhythm.",[("flared serif",0.12,0.3),("round O",0.25,0.95),("Madrid, 1846",0.85,0.85)]),
("ralph-lauren","Ralph Lauren","https://www.ralphlauren.com/","Ralph Lauren started the company in New York in 1967 by selling neckties under the name Polo.","Widely spaced serif capitals give the founder's name a classic, Ivy League feel.","The famous Polo pony is a separate sub-brand mark, so the main wordmark stays purely typographic.",[("spaced serif caps",0.18,0.3),("Ivy League",0.6,0.15),("pony on Polo only",0.82,0.88)]),
("calvin-klein","Calvin Klein","https://www.calvinklein.us/","Calvin Klein and Barry Schwartz founded the company in New York in 1968.","A clean geometric sans serif makes the founder's name look modern and minimal.","Tight, even spacing lets the logo work as large as a billboard and as small as a waistband.",[("geometric sans",0.18,0.3),("minimal",0.6,0.15),("waistband ready",0.82,0.88)]),
("tommy-hilfiger","Tommy Hilfiger","https://usa.tommy.com/","Tommy Hilfiger launched his label in New York in 1985.","The small flag in red, white, and navy has become the brand's most recognizable element.","Spaced capitals on both sides of the flag give the logo a preppy, American look.",[("flag mark",0.5,0.1),("red, white, navy",0.5,0.95),("spaced caps",0.15,0.3)]),
("marc-jacobs","Marc Jacobs","https://www.marcjacobs.com/","Marc Jacobs founded his label in New York in 1984.","Very wide letter spacing turns the founder's name into a clean, airy wordmark.","Geometric capitals with no decoration let the logo sit easily on bags, perfume, and labels.",[("wide spacing",0.18,0.3),("geometric caps",0.6,0.15),("founder's name",0.82,0.85)]),
("alexander-mcqueen","Alexander McQueen","https://www.alexandermcqueen.com/","Lee Alexander McQueen founded his label in London in 1992, and the brand now signs its logo simply as McQueen.","The small c set inside the Q is a playful detail that makes the short name memorable.","Wide serif capitals balance the brand's dark, theatrical image with classic tailoring.",[("c inside the Q",0.18,0.85),("wide serif caps",0.75,0.15),("shorter name",0.82,0.88)]),
("stella-mccartney","Stella McCartney","https://www.stellamccartney.com/","Stella McCartney launched her label in 2001, and it has never used leather or fur.","The letters are drawn with dots, giving the logo a light, almost stitched feel.","The very wide spacing and thin construction make the wordmark feel gentle and modern.",[("dotted letters",0.18,0.3),("stitched feel",0.6,0.15),("thin and wide",0.82,0.88)]),
("vivienne-westwood","Vivienne Westwood","https://www.viviennewestwood.com/","Vivienne Westwood opened her first shop with Malcolm McLaren on London's King's Road in 1971.","The bold, slanted serif script has the attitude of the brand's punk roots.","The two names stack on top of each other, so the logo works like a badge or a label.",[("punk roots",0.18,0.3),("slanted serif",0.75,0.15),("stacked names",0.7,0.9)]),
("paul-smith","Paul Smith","https://www.paulsmith.com/","Paul Smith opened his first shop in Nottingham, England, in 1970.","The logo is based on Paul Smith's own handwriting, so it feels personal and friendly.","A signature-style logo suits a brand known for playful details and colourful stripes.",[("his handwriting",0.18,0.3),("signature",0.7,0.15),("friendly",0.7,0.9)]),
("hugo-boss","Hugo Boss","https://www.hugoboss.com/","Hugo Boss was founded in Metzingen, Germany, in 1924, and in 2021 the main line was rebranded simply as BOSS.","The 2021 wordmark is heavy, wide, and all caps, designed to stand out on social media.","Shortening the name to four letters made the logo bolder and easier to read at small sizes.",[("2021 rebrand",0.18,0.3),("heavy caps",0.6,0.15),("four letters",0.82,0.88)]),
("jimmy-choo","Jimmy Choo","https://www.jimmychoo.com/","Jimmy Choo was co-founded in London in 1996 by shoemaker Jimmy Choo and Tamara Mellon.","Thin, wide capitals give the founder's name a light, elegant feel, like a stiletto heel.","The wordmark keeps the brand looking polished on shoe boxes and soles.",[("thin caps",0.18,0.3),("like a stiletto",0.6,0.15),("founder's name",0.82,0.85)]),
("christian-louboutin","Christian Louboutin","https://www.christianlouboutin.com/","Christian Louboutin founded his shoe brand in Paris in 1991, and its red lacquered soles became a signature.","The logo is a flowing signature, which makes the brand feel personal and handmade.","A small \"Christian\" sits above a large, swirling surname with a long flourish.",[("small \"Christian\"",0.3,0.05),("signature script",0.65,0.55),("long flourish",0.2,0.95)]),
("coach","Coach","https://www.coach.com/","Coach was founded in New York in 1941 as a family-run leather workshop.","The frame around the name looks like a stamped leather tag, a nod to the brand's craft.","Heavy serif capitals make the short name feel solid and durable.",[("leather tag frame",0.03,0.5),("heavy serif",0.5,0.4),("New York, 1941",0.9,0.9)]),
("michael-kors","Michael Kors","https://www.michaelkors.com/","Michael Kors launched his label in New York in 1981.","A clean, geometric sans serif makes the founder's name easy to read on bags and watches.","The even, generous spacing keeps the logo modern and approachable.",[("clean sans",0.18,0.3),("founder's name",0.6,0.15),("even spacing",0.82,0.85)]),
("kate-spade","Kate Spade","https://www.katespade.com/","Kate and Andy Spade founded the brand in New York in 1993, starting with handbags.","The spade symbol is a witty play on the founder's surname.","The lowercase serif wordmark and small \"new york\" line make the logo feel friendly and feminine.",[("spade symbol",0.5,0.05),("lowercase serif",0.3,0.6),("new york",0.5,0.98)]),
("tory-burch","Tory Burch","https://www.toryburch.com/","Tory Burch launched her label in New York in 2004.","The double T medallion between the names works as a monogram on hardware, shoes, and bags.","Wide capitals on each side make the logo symmetrical and balanced.",[("double T",0.5,0.3),("medallion",0.5,0.95),("wide caps",0.1,0.3)]),
("longchamp","Longchamp","https://www.longchamp.com/","Jean Cassegrain founded Longchamp in Paris in 1948, naming it after the Longchamp racecourse.","Very wide letter spacing gives the name a light, elegant feel.","The small \"Paris\" line underneath connects the brand to its French origins.",[("wide spacing",0.18,0.3),("Paris",0.5,0.95),("thin sans",0.82,0.3)]),
("ferragamo","Ferragamo","https://www.ferragamo.com/","Salvatore Ferragamo founded the brand in Florence in 1927, and in 2022 the house dropped \"Salvatore\" with a new wordmark by Peter Saville.","The 2022 logo replaced the founder's signature with clean, wide capitals.","Dropping the first name and the script made the brand feel younger and more modern.",[("\"Salvatore\" dropped",0.18,0.3),("Peter Saville, 2022",0.6,0.15),("wide caps",0.82,0.85)]),
("miu-miu","Miu Miu","https://www.miumiu.com/","Miuccia Prada founded Miu Miu in 1993, naming it after her childhood nickname.","Rounded, chunky letters make the logo look playful and youthful.","Repeating the same word creates a pattern, like a label on a school uniform.",[("rounded letters",0.18,0.3),("Miuccia's nickname",0.6,0.15),("repeated word",0.75,0.85)]),
("off-white","Off-White","https://www.off---white.com/","Virgil Abloh founded Off-White in Milan in 2013.","A plain, bold sans serif looks like a label on industrial packaging, which fits the brand's ironic style.","The trademark symbol is part of the logo, turning a legal mark into a design detail.",[("bold sans",0.18,0.3),("hyphen",0.43,0.55),("™ as design",0.95,0.1)]),
("supreme","Supreme","https://supreme.com/","James Jebbia opened the first Supreme store in New York in 1994.","White Futura Heavy Oblique on a red box makes the logo instantly recognizable.","The box style was inspired by the work of artist Barbara Kruger.",[("red box",0.08,0.1),("Futura oblique",0.3,0.6),("Barbara Kruger",0.92,0.95)]),
("stussy","Stüssy","https://www.stussy.com/","Shawn Stussy founded the brand in Laguna Beach, California, in 1980, starting with surfboards.","The logo is his graffiti-style signature, the same one he wrote on his surfboards.","The rough, hand-drawn strokes gave streetwear its look long before it was mainstream.",[("graffiti signature",0.5,0.3),("surfboard roots",0.4,0.6),("hand-drawn",0.85,0.8)]),
("moncler","Moncler","https://www.moncler.com/","Moncler was founded in 1952 in Monestier-de-Clermont, near Grenoble, and its name is an abbreviation of that town.","The thin, wide capitals feel light and premium, like the brand's down jackets.","The name itself tells the brand's mountain origin story.",[("town abbreviated",0.25,0.3),("thin caps",0.6,0.15),("mountain heritage",0.82,0.88)]),
("acne-studios","Acne Studios","https://www.acnestudios.com/","Acne Studios was founded in Stockholm in 1996, and Acne stands for \"Ambition to Create Novel Expressions\".","The rounded sans serif looks friendly and slightly quirky, like the brand itself.","The full name, with \"Studios\", reflects the brand's start as a creative collective.",[("acronym",0.12,0.3),("rounded sans",0.6,0.15),("Stockholm, 1996",0.82,0.88)]),
("zara","Zara","https://www.zara.com/","Amancio Ortega opened the first Zara store in A Coruña, Spain, in 1975, and the current logo was introduced in 2019.","The overlapping letters of the 2019 logo were designed by Baron & Baron, the agency behind many luxury brands.","The high-contrast Didone serif makes a high-street brand look like a fashion magazine.",[("overlapping letters",0.5,0.3),("Didone serif",0.12,0.9),("2019 redesign",0.88,0.92)]),
("h-and-m","H&M","https://www2.hm.com/","H&M started as Hennes, a women's clothing store in Västerås, Sweden, in 1947.","The red, handwritten-style letters make the logo look friendly and fast.","The initials stand for Hennes & Mauritz, after the brand bought the Mauritz Widforss store in 1968.",[("red script",0.18,0.3),("Hennes & Mauritz",0.5,0.92),("italic",0.82,0.15)]),
("uniqlo","Uniqlo","https://www.uniqlo.com/","Uniqlo opened its first store in Hiroshima, Japan, in 1984, and its current logo was designed by Kashiwa Sato in 2006.","Two red squares hold the name split into two lines, in English and in Japanese katakana.","The square format works as an app icon, a shop sign, and a shopping bag print.",[("red square",0.08,0.1),("name in two lines",0.3,0.75),("Kashiwa Sato",0.92,0.95)]),
("levis","Levi's","https://www.levi.com/","Levi Strauss founded the company in San Francisco in 1853, and the batwing logo dates from the late 1960s.","The batwing shape is based on the arched stitching on the back pocket of Levi's jeans.","Bold white letters on red link to the small red tab sewn on every pair of jeans.",[("batwing shape",0.5,0.95),("pocket stitching",0.12,0.2),("red tab",0.85,0.2)]),
]
assert len(B)==45
